From c4d1bf879ab14e96b7c7f754fbcb4e2885510e91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Audia <therealgraysky@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:01:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] kernel: bump 6.18 to 6.18.57

Changelog: https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/ChangeLog-6.18.57

Removed upstreamed:
  linux/generic/backport-6.18/948-v7.1-net-dsa-mt7530-fix-.get_stats64-sleeping-in-atomic-c.patch[1]
  linux/rockchip/patches-6.18/045-15-v7.0-media-v4l2-mem2mem-Add-a-kref-to-the-v4l2_m2m_dev-structure.patch[2]
  linux/rockchip/patches-6.18/045-16-v7.0-media-verisilicon-Avoid-G2-bus-error-while-decoding-H.264-an.patch[3]
  linux/rockchip/patches-6.18/045-43-v7.0-media-verisilicon-Fix-kernel-panic-due-to-__initconst-misuse.patch[4]

Manually rebased:
  linux/generic/backport-6.18/706-03-v7.2-netfilter-flowtable-bail-out-if-forward-path-cannot-b.patch
  linux/bcm27xx/patches-6.18/0351-brcmfmac-Fix-interoperating-DPP-and-other-encryption.patch

All other patches automatically rebased via update_kernel.sh

mac80211: 6.18.57 backports struct sockaddr_unsized[5], so add
160-backports-sockaddr_unsized-is-in-6.18.57.patch to only define it
in backports for older kernels.

kernel: 6.18.57 makes rpcsec_gss_krb5 use crypto/krb5[6], so add
kmod-crypto-krb5 and make kmod-fs-nfs-common-rpcsec depend on it.

ltq-ifxos: 6.18.57 converts proto_ops bind() to sockaddr_unsized[5],
so cast the bind address accordingly on 6.18.57+.

